 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our ADK booking agent has a tool `reserve_table()` that POSTs to the restaurant partner API. Their API is garbage: sometimes it takes 40s and our httpx client times out at 30, but the reservation actually went through. The agent then retries and we get duplicate bookings. Twice last week a customer showed up to find two tables held under their name lol. How do I make this safe? Partner doesn't support idempotency keys afaik. Running on Cloud Run, Python 3.12."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Need a design review before Friday's demo. Flow: the agent proposes a refund, the user clicks approve/decline in our UI (we use ADK's tool confirmation thing), then `issue_refund` calls Stripe. Concerns: (1) if the container restarts between approval and the Stripe call, does the refund get lost or replayed? (2) if the user declines but the LLM decides to call the tool again on the next turn, what stops it? (3) which Stripe errors are safe to retry? I want approved = happens exactly once, declined = never happens. Sketch the state handling + retry logic pls."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "our payments agent keeps hitting 429s from the Vertex AI Gemini endpoint during peak hours and the whole conversation just dies with a ResourceExhausted error. I tried wrapping in tenacity but it still fails. Is there a way to bump the quota or should we be spreading across regions? Project is on us-central1 only right now.", "needs_instead": "Help with Vertex AI model quota and rate limits: requesting quota increases, using provisioned throughput or multi-region/global endpoints, and backoff for LLM calls. This is not about making external side-effecting HTTP writes idempotent or enforcing approved-exactly-once."}
